module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SplittingPrinciple.ChernRootsTotal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SplittingPrinciple.ChernRootPowerSums
public import Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset
public import Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Subring.Basic
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# `P_p` of the Chern classes as an element of the ring of graded cap families

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project, Stacks 02QL, let `X` be
locally of finite type over `S`, and let `P_p` be the universal power-sum polynomial of
Stacks 0F9B. For a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` of rank `r` the Chern classes
`c_i(ℱ) ∩ -` are the homogeneous components

  `c_i(ℱ) = Stacks.Chow.homComponent i (Stacks.Chow.GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX ℱ r)`

of the total Chern class, in the ring `Stacks.Chow.GradedCapFamily (Stacks.Chow.chowGroup C sX)`.
That ring is **not commutative**, while `AlgebraicGeometry.powerSumOfChernClasses` — the value of
`P_p` at a rank and a family of Chern classes — is an evaluation of a polynomial and needs a
commutative ring. This file supplies the commutative ring: **the subring generated by all the
Chern classes of all finite locally free modules on `X`**.

Any two of those classes commute, which is Stacks 02UA read componentwise
(`Stacks.Chow.commute_homComponent_chernFamily`), so
`Subring.isMulCommutative_closure` makes `Stacks.Chow.chernSubring` a commutative ring, and

  `Stacks.Chow.powerSumChernElem C sX ℱ r p = P_p(c_1(ℱ), …, c_p(ℱ))`

is defined there and read back in the ambient ring.

## The splitting principle inside the subring

In the subring, `AlgebraicGeometry.HasChernRoots` — the hypothesis that a rank and a family of
Chern classes are the number and the elementary symmetric functions of a family of roots — can be
*verified*, from the product formulae of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SplittingPrinciple.ChernRootsTotal`:

* `Stacks.Chow.hasChernRoots_of_hasQuotients` — if `ℰ` carries a filtration of length `r` with
  invertible successive quotients `ℒ_i`, the Chern roots of `ℰ` are the `c₁(ℒ_i)`. This is
  Stacks 02UJ, `Stacks.Chow.chernFamily_eq_prod_of_hasQuotients`, read coefficientwise;
* `Stacks.Chow.hasChernRoots_tensorObj_of_hasQuotients` — the Chern roots of `ℰ₁ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℰ₂` are
  the `r · s` sums `c₁(ℒ_i) + c₁(𝒩_j)`. This is
  `Stacks.Chow.chernFamily_tensorObj_eq_prod_prod` read coefficientwise.

Reading a product `∏_i (1 + x_i)` of one-plus-a-degree-one-class coefficientwise is
`Stacks.Chow.homComponent_map_prod_one_add`: the index-`k` component of such a product is the
`k`-th elementary symmetric function of the `x_i`, because a product of `k` classes of index one
is homogeneous of index `k`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.chernComponents`, `Stacks.Chow.chernSubring` — the set of all Chern-class
  components of all finite locally free modules, and the subring it generates. The subring is
  commutative.
* `Stacks.Chow.chernClassSub`, `Stacks.Chow.firstChernSub` — `c_i(ℱ)` and `c₁(ℒ)` as elements of
  that subring.
* `Stacks.Chow.powerSumChernElem` — `P_p(c_1(ℱ), …, c_p(ℱ))` as an element of the ring of graded
  cap families.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.commute_homComponent_chernFamily` — Stacks 02UA componentwise: any two Chern
  classes of any two finite locally free modules commute.
* `Stacks.Chow.homComponent_map_prod_one_add` — the coefficients of `∏_i (1 + x_i)` are the
  elementary symmetric functions of the `x_i`.
* `Stacks.Chow.hasChernRoots_of_hasQuotients`,
  `Stacks.Chow.hasChernRoots_tensorObj_of_hasQuotients` — the Chern roots of a filtered module
  and of a tensor product of two filtered modules.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F9B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F9B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02QL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QL)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### Coefficients of a product of one-plus-a-class, in a commutative realization -/

section Algebra

universe v

variable {G : ℤ → Type v} [∀ k, AddCommGroup (G k)]

/-- Two homogeneous components commute as soon as the two components in question commute
termwise, up to the transport comparing `k - i - j` with `k - j - i`. -/
theorem commute_homComponent_of_comm_apply {a b : GradedCapFamily G} {i j : ℕ}
    (h : ∀ (k : ℤ) (x : G k),
      a (k - (j : ℤ)) i (b k j x) =
        gradedDegreeCast G (show k - (i : ℤ) - (j : ℤ) = k - (j : ℤ) - (i : ℤ) by ring)
          (b (k - (i : ℤ)) j (a k i x))) :
    Commute (homComponent i a) (homComponent j b) := by
  refine commute_of_comm_apply fun k i' j' x => ?_
  by_cases hj' : j' = j
  · subst hj'
    by_cases hi' : i' = i
    · subst hi'
      simpa using h k x
    · rw [homComponent_apply_of_ne hi' a, homComponent_apply_of_ne hi' a]
      simp
  · rw [homComponent_apply_of_ne hj' b, homComponent_apply_of_ne hj' b]
    simp

variable {A : Type v} [CommRing A] (f : A →+* GradedCapFamily G)

/-- A product of `t.card` classes of index one has index `t.card`. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_map_prod {ι : Type*} {x : ι → A}
    (hx : ∀ i, (f (x i)).IsHomogeneous 1) (t : Finset ι) :
    (f (∏ i ∈ t, x i)).IsHomogeneous t.card := by
  classical
  induction t using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simpa using GradedCapFamily.IsHomogeneous.one
  | insert a t ha ih =>
      rw [Finset.prod_insert ha, map_mul, Finset.card_insert_of_notMem ha, Nat.add_comm]
      exact (hx a).mul ih

/-- The `k`-th elementary symmetric function of roots is the sum of the products over the
`k`-element subsets. -/
private theorem esymmOfRoots_eq_sum_prod {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (x : ι → A)
    (k : ℕ) : AlgebraicGeometry.esymmOfRoots x k
      = ∑ t ∈ Finset.powersetCard k (Finset.univ : Finset ι), ∏ i ∈ t, x i :=
  Finset.esymm_map_val x _ k

/-- The `k`-th elementary symmetric function of a family of classes of index one has index `k`. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_map_esymmOfRoots {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {x : ι → A}
    (hx : ∀ i, (f (x i)).IsHomogeneous 1) (k : ℕ) :
    (f (AlgebraicGeometry.esymmOfRoots x k)).IsHomogeneous k := by
  classical
  rw [esymmOfRoots_eq_sum_prod, map_sum]
  exact GradedCapFamily.IsHomogeneous.sum fun t ht =>
    (Finset.mem_powersetCard.mp ht).2 ▸ isHomogeneous_map_prod f hx t

/-- **The coefficients of `∏_i (1 + x_i)` are the elementary symmetric functions of the `x_i`.**
For classes `x_i` of index one the index-`k` component of the product is `e_k(x)`. -/
theorem homComponent_map_prod_one_add {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {x : ι → A}
    (hx : ∀ i, (f (x i)).IsHomogeneous 1) (k : ℕ) :
    homComponent k (f (∏ i, (1 + x i))) = f (AlgebraicGeometry.esymmOfRoots x k) := by
  classical
  have hprod : (∏ i, ((1 : A) + x i))
      = ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (Fintype.card ι + 1), AlgebraicGeometry.esymmOfRoots x j := by
    rw [Finset.prod_one_add, Finset.sum_powerset, Finset.card_univ]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => (esymmOfRoots_eq_sum_prod x j).symm
  rw [hprod, map_sum, map_sum, Finset.sum_eq_single k]
  · exact (isHomogeneous_map_esymmOfRoots f hx k).homComponent_self
  · intro j _ hjk
    exact (isHomogeneous_map_esymmOfRoots f hx j).homComponent_of_ne (Ne.symm hjk)
  · intro hk
    have hlt : Fintype.card ι < k := by
      simpa [Finset.mem_range] using hk
    have hz : AlgebraicGeometry.esymmOfRoots x k = 0 := by
      simp only [AlgebraicGeometry.esymmOfRoots]
      exact Multiset.esymm_of_card_lt (by simpa using hlt)
    rw [hz, map_zero, map_zero]

/-- **The splitting principle verified in a commutative realization.** If an injective ring
homomorphism `f` carries `∏_i (1 + x_i)` to the total Chern class `u`, each `f x_i` having index
one, and carries `c_i` to the index-`i` component of `u`, then the rank and the family `c` have
the `x_i` as Chern roots. -/
theorem hasChernRoots_of_map_prod_one_add {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (hf : Function.Injective f)
    {x : ι → A} (hx : ∀ i, (f (x i)).IsHomogeneous 1) {u : GradedCapFamily G}
    (hu : f (∏ i, (1 + x i)) = u) {r : ℕ} (hr : r = Fintype.card ι) {c : ℕ+ → A}
    (hc : ∀ i : ℕ+, f (c i) = homComponent (i : ℕ) u) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.HasChernRoots r c x where
  rank := hr
  chernClass i := by
    refine hf ?_
    rw [hc i, ← hu]
    exact homComponent_map_prod_one_add f hx (i : ℕ)

/-- A ring homomorphism carries a product over `Fin r` to the ordered product of the images, read
as a `List.prod` because the target need not be commutative. -/
private theorem map_prod_fin {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A) :
    f (∏ i, a i) = (List.ofFn fun i => f (a i)).prod := by
  rw [← Fin.prod_ofFn a, map_list_prod, List.map_ofFn]
  simp [Function.comp_def]

/-- A ring homomorphism carries a product `∏_{i < r} (1 + w_i)` to the ordered product of the
images, read as a `List.prod` because the target need not be commutative. -/
theorem map_prod_one_add {r : ℕ} (w : Fin r → A) :
    f (∏ i, (1 + w i)) = (List.ofFn fun i => 1 + f (w i)).prod := by
  simpa using map_prod_fin f fun i => 1 + w i

/-- A ring homomorphism carries the product `∏_{i, j} (1 + (v_i + w_j))` over a product of index
types to the iterated ordered product of the images. -/
theorem map_prod_prod_one_add {r s : ℕ} (v : Fin r → A) (w : Fin s → A) :
    f (∏ ij : Fin r × Fin s, (1 + (v ij.1 + w ij.2)))
      = (List.ofFn fun i => (List.ofFn fun j => 1 + (f (v i) + f (w j))).prod).prod := by
  rw [Fintype.prod_prod_type, map_prod_fin]
  refine congrArg List.prod (congrArg List.ofFn (funext fun i => ?_))
  simpa using map_prod_one_add f fun j => v i + w j

end Algebra

/-! ### Stacks 02UA componentwise -/

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- **Stacks 02UA componentwise.** The `i`-th Chern class of one finite locally free module and
the `j`-th Chern class of another commute in the ring of graded cap families. -/
theorem commute_homComponent_chernFamily (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    (F : X.Modules) (s : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F s] (i j : ℕ) :
    Commute (homComponent i (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX E r))
      (homComponent j (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F s)) :=
  commute_homComponent_of_comm_apply fun k x => comm_apply_chernFamily C sX E r F s k i j x

/-! ### The commutative subring generated by the Chern classes -/

/-- The set of all homogeneous components of the total Chern classes of all finite locally free
`𝒪_X`-modules of constant rank: the Chern classes `c_i(ℱ) ∩ -` read as graded cap families. -/
def chernComponents : Set (GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX)) :=
  {a | ∃ (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
        (hF : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r) (i : ℕ),
        a = homComponent i (@GenuineChern.chernFamily C X sX ‹_› F r hF)}

/-- **The subring generated by the Chern classes.** Unlike the ring of graded cap families, it is
commutative (`Stacks.Chow.isMulCommutative_chernSubring`). -/
abbrev chernSubring : Subring (GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX)) :=
  Subring.closure (chernComponents C sX)

/-- Every Chern class of every finite locally free module lies in the subring. -/
theorem homComponent_chernFamily_mem_chernSubring (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r] (i : ℕ) :
    homComponent i (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F r) ∈ chernSubring C sX :=
  Subring.subset_closure ⟨F, r, inferInstance, i, rfl⟩

/-- **The subring generated by the Chern classes is commutative**, which is Stacks 02UA
componentwise. -/
instance isMulCommutative_chernSubring : IsMulCommutative (chernSubring C sX) :=
  Subring.isMulCommutative_closure fun a ha b hb _ => by
    obtain ⟨E, r, hE, i, rfl⟩ := ha
    obtain ⟨F, s, hF, j, rfl⟩ := hb
    exact @commute_homComponent_chernFamily C X sX _ E r hE F s hF i j

open scoped IsMulCommutative in
/-- The subring generated by the Chern classes, as a commutative ring. -/
instance instCommRingChernSubring : CommRing (chernSubring C sX) := inferInstance

/-- **The `i`-th Chern class of a finite locally free module as an element of the commutative
subring.** -/
def chernClassSub (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r] (i : ℕ) :
    chernSubring C sX :=
  ⟨homComponent i (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F r),
    homComponent_chernFamily_mem_chernSubring C sX F r i⟩

@[simp]
theorem coe_chernClassSub (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r] (i : ℕ) :
    ((chernClassSub C sX F r i : chernSubring C sX) : GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX))
      = homComponent i (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F r) :=
  rfl

attribute [local instance] isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isInvertible

/-- **The first Chern class of a module of rank one as an element of the commutative subring.** -/
def firstChernSub (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} L 1] :
    chernSubring C sX :=
  chernClassSub C sX L 1 1

@[simp]
theorem coe_firstChernSub (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} L 1] :
    ((firstChernSub C sX L : chernSubring C sX) : GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX))
      = firstChernElem C sX L :=
  rfl

/-- **`P_p` of the Chern classes of a finite locally free module**, as an element of the ring of
graded cap families on the Chow groups of `X`: the value of the universal power-sum polynomial of
Stacks 0F9B at the rank and the Chern classes `c_1(ℱ), …, c_p(ℱ)`, computed in the commutative
subring they generate. In degree zero it is the rank and in degree one it is `c_1(ℱ)`. -/
def powerSumChernElem (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r] (p : ℕ) :
    GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX) :=
  ((AlgebraicGeometry.powerSumOfChernClasses (A := chernSubring C sX) r
    (fun i : ℕ+ => chernClassSub C sX F r (i : ℕ)) p : chernSubring C sX) :
      GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX))

/-- **`P_0(ℱ)` is the rank of `ℱ`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem powerSumChernElem_zero (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r] :
    powerSumChernElem C sX F r 0 = (r : GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX)) := by
  simp only [powerSumChernElem, AlgebraicGeometry.powerSumOfChernClasses_zero]
  exact map_natCast (Subring.subtype (chernSubring C sX)) r

/-- **`P_1(ℱ)` is the first Chern class of `ℱ`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem powerSumChernElem_one (F : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r] :
    powerSumChernElem C sX F r 1 = homComponent 1 (GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F r) := by
  simp only [powerSumChernElem, AlgebraicGeometry.powerSumOfChernClasses_one]
  rfl

/-- Isomorphic modules, of ranks spelled differently but equal, have the same Chern classes in
the commutative subring. -/
theorem chernClassSub_congr {F F' : X.Modules} {r r' : ℕ}
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F' r'] (e : F' ≅ F)
    (h : r' = r) (i : ℕ) : chernClassSub C sX F' r' i = chernClassSub C sX F r i :=
  Subtype.ext (by
    rw [coe_chernClassSub, coe_chernClassSub, GenuineChern.chernFamily_congr C sX F r e h])

/-- Isomorphic modules, of ranks spelled differently but equal, have the same `P_p`. -/
theorem powerSumChernElem_congr {F F' : X.Modules} {r r' : ℕ}
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F' r'] (e : F' ≅ F)
    (h : r' = r) (p : ℕ) : powerSumChernElem C sX F' r' p = powerSumChernElem C sX F r p := by
  simp only [powerSumChernElem, chernClassSub_congr C sX e h]
  rw [h]

/-! ### The Chern roots of a filtered module and of a tensor product -/

section Filtration

/-- `hasChernRoots_of_map_prod_one_add` for the inclusion of the Chern subring, where `c` is a
family of Chern classes of a module of rank `r` with total Chern class `u`. -/
private theorem hasChernRoots_chernSubring {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {x : ι → chernSubring C sX}
    (hx : ∀ i, ((x i : chernSubring C sX) : GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX)).IsHomogeneous 1)
    {F : X.Modules} {r : ℕ}
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} F r]
    (hu : (chernSubring C sX).subtype (∏ i, (1 + x i)) = GenuineChern.chernFamily C sX F r)
    (hr : r = Fintype.card ι) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.HasChernRoots r (fun i : ℕ+ => chernClassSub C sX F r (i : ℕ)) x :=
  hasChernRoots_of_map_prod_one_add _ (fun _ _ hab => Subtype.ext hab) hx hu hr fun _ => rfl

/-- **The Chern roots of a filtered module, Stacks 02UJ read coefficientwise.** If `ℰ` carries a
filtration of length `r` whose successive quotients are the invertible modules `ℒ_i`, then in the
commutative subring generated by the Chern classes the rank `r` and the Chern classes of `ℰ` have
the `c₁(ℒ_i)` as Chern roots: `c_k(ℰ) = e_k(c₁(ℒ_1), …, c₁(ℒ_r))`. -/
theorem hasChernRoots_of_hasQuotients (r : ℕ) (E : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r]
    (L : Fin r → X.Modules)
    [∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property (L i)]
    (h : HasQuotients X r E L) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.HasChernRoots r (fun i : ℕ+ => chernClassSub C sX E r (i : ℕ))
      (fun i : Fin r => firstChernSub C sX (L i)) := by
  refine hasChernRoots_chernSubring C sX (fun i => isHomogeneous_firstChernElem C sX (L i)) ?_
    (Fintype.card_fin r).symm
  rw [map_prod_one_add]
  exact (chernFamily_eq_prod_of_hasQuotients C sX r E L h).symm

/-- **The Chern roots of a tensor product are the sums of the Chern roots.** If `ℰ₁` carries a
filtration of length `r` with invertible successive quotients `ℒ_i` and `ℰ₂` one of length `s`
with invertible successive quotients `𝒩_j`, then the rank `t = r · s` and the Chern classes of
`ℰ₁ ⊗_{𝒪_X} ℰ₂` have the `r · s` classes `c₁(ℒ_i) + c₁(𝒩_j)` as Chern roots. -/
theorem hasChernRoots_tensorObj_of_hasQuotients (r s t : ℕ) (E₁ E₂ : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E₁ r]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E₂ s]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (Scheme.Modules.tensorObj E₁ E₂) t]
    (L : Fin r → X.Modules)
    [hL : ∀ i, AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property
      (L i)]
    (N : Fin s → X.Modules)
    [∀ j, AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property (N j)]
    (h₁ : HasQuotients X r E₁ L) (h₂ : HasQuotients X s E₂ N) (ht : t = r * s) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.HasChernRoots t
      (fun i : ℕ+ => chernClassSub C sX (Scheme.Modules.tensorObj E₁ E₂) t (i : ℕ))
      (fun ij : Fin r × Fin s => firstChernSub C sX (L ij.1) + firstChernSub C sX (N ij.2)) := by
  refine hasChernRoots_chernSubring C sX (fun ij => ?_) ?_ (by rw [ht]; simp)
  · exact (isHomogeneous_firstChernElem C sX (L ij.1)).add
      (isHomogeneous_firstChernElem C sX (N ij.2))
  · rw [map_prod_prod_one_add ((chernSubring C sX).subtype)
        (fun i => firstChernSub C sX (L i)) (fun j => firstChernSub C sX (N j)),
      chernFamily_tensorObj_eq_prod_prod C sX r s t E₁ E₂ L N h₁ h₂ ht]
    refine congrArg List.prod (congrArg List.ofFn (funext fun i => ?_))
    refine congrArg List.prod (congrArg List.ofFn (funext fun j => ?_))
    exact congrArg (fun z => (1 : GradedCapFamily (chowGroup C sX)) + z)
      (add_comm (firstChernElem C sX (L i)) (firstChernElem C sX (N j)))

end Filtration

end Stacks.Chow

end
